# {{.Name}}

A [PlatformKit](https://github.com/septagon-oss/platformkit) application — one
Go binary that composes a nine-module multi-tenant SaaS starter (auth, users,
tenants, API keys, audit, content, notifications, health, and an admin console)
and mounts your own modules beside it. Server-rendered HTML, no Node, no
frontend build.

## Run it

```bash
go run .
```

Boots a zero-config development instance at http://127.0.0.1:8080/admin with a
seeded local tenant and administrator (the login prints on first boot).

## Add a module

```bash
platformkit new module invoice
make verify
```

The module registers itself — no wiring. It's tenant-scoped, authorized, and
ships with a test. See [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md) for the rules that keep a module
correct (they apply to humans and AI agents alike).

## Deploy

Production is signalled by the presence of `config.yaml`:

```bash
cp config.example.yaml config.yaml         # edit addr, db, email
export PK_ADMIN_PASSWORD='a-long-random-secret'
go build -o {{.Name}} . && ./{{.Name}}
```

The admin password comes from the environment, never `config.yaml`. Or with
containers:

```bash
PK_ADMIN_PASSWORD='...' docker compose up --build
```

## Commands

| Command | What |
|---|---|
| `go run .` | Boot a development instance |
| `platformkit new module <name>` | Scaffold a tenant-scoped module |
| `platformkit modules --json` | List composed modules |
| `platformkit openapi` | Print the OpenAPI document |
| `make verify` | `go vet` + `go test -race ./...` |

## Layout

```
main.go        boots the starter with your modules
modules.go     the additive module registry
mod_*.go       your modules (each self-registers)
migrations/    append-only SQL migrations
config.example.yaml   deployment config template
AGENTS.md      the contract for extending safely
```
